Included skill paths:
- finance/skills/financial-statements/SKILL.md
- finance/skills/reconciliation/SKILL.md
- finance/skills/variance-analysis/SKILL.md
- finance/skills/journal-entry/SKILL.md

The close-package web app in this repository is a derivative implementation of
those skills' workflows, formats, checklists, and materiality guidance.
Extracted SKILL.md copies add a short attribution banner and point connector
placeholders at CONNECTORS.md. They are modified files under Section 4(b) of
the Apache License: FA Foundry further changed them by adding Foundry runtime
notes and analysis-mode sections, adding "do not use" clauses to their
descriptions, adding guard sentences (journal entries are drafts only; no ERP
or data-warehouse connection is claimed unless the session configures one;
no posting or payment), and renaming slash commands to the bundled skill names.

Report visual method adaptations
===============================

Foundry's method/report-visuals.md and report visual implementation adapt
selected layout and editorial principles from these MIT-licensed works:

- diagram-design, https://github.com/cathrynlavery/diagram-design
  Revision: cea465e7f5ea1043d8dab21a99f2dd3f7f661beb
  References: skills/diagram-design/SKILL.md and bar, line, process type notes.
  Adapted: relation-first type selection, density, semantic color roles,
  self-contained SVG, direct labels and connector spacing.
- huashu-report, https://github.com/alchaincyf/huashu-report
  Revision: bdc08bee5077462e1300431408c5237438a22d00
  References: SKILL.md and references/图表模式库.md.
  Adapted: reader-oriented chart choice, direct labels, figure/takeaway/unit/
  source organization, negative-value, missing-value and zero-baseline checks.

The upstream scripts, full visual catalogues and runtime workflows are not
bundled. Foundry uses its own renderer, theme, fonts and task-owned evidence
model. The MIT terms below apply to each adapted upstream work; the Apache-2.0
notice above continues to apply to the existing finance method copies.

